<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose seven points to 1,257.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose seven points to 1,257.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,257 today from 1,250 on June 10, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1316    11.950	  1308    11.875</p>
<p>   1a   1246  9436.000	  1225  9281.000</p>
<p>   2    1474    21.057	  1468    20.975</p>
<p>   2a   1399 11471.000	  1385 11356.000</p>
<p>   3    1312    12.107	  1307    12.056</p>
<p>   3a   1132  8936.000	  1119  8831.000</p>
<p>   6    1288    13.286	  1286    13.269</p>
<p>   7    1178     6.221	  1281     6.238</p>
<p>   8     818     8.993	   819     9.006</p>
<p>   9     705  6164.000	   703  6144.000</p>
<p>  10    1181     5.964	  1183     5.975</p>
